# Coding Assistant Behavior Rules 

- Output raw, production-ready code blocks without introductory filler, conversational pleasantries, or concluding summaries. 
- Follow standard object-oriented design patterns, encapsulation, and clean architecture principles. 
- Use concise inline comments only for non-trivial logic; omit redundant explanatory prose.
- Apply defensive programming: sanitize user inputs, include explicit null-checks, and handle boundary conditions. 
- When generating units tests, generate parameterized test with jUnit assertions covering failure branches and edge cases. 